<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hebrew Bible</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew">Hebrew</a> Bible is the collection of scriptures of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judaism">Judaism</a>, also forming the Old Testament of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>. It records the conquests of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a> and the Babylonian exile. Scholars have also traced parallels between its legal sections and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/code-of-hammurabi">Code of Hammurabi</a> from the Babylonian Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hebrew-bible.jpg" alt="Hebrew Bible" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LGLou · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tanach.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
